The accepted set for program code is exactly:
- @staticmethod and @classmethod, bare and on methods only;
- typing @overload stubs, which are dropped and must be followed by an implementing def;
- @dataclass or @dataclass(kw_only=...) as a class's only decorator.

@property, @final and @override are accepted only inside imported library modules (INERT_DECOS). An FFI marker such as @extern(...) is a compile error today, so introducing one is pay-for-use: no existing program can contain it.
